DESCRIPTION >
    Sessions: raw conversion rows over a caller-supplied range, to mark
    converting sessions during on-read session derivation. Tenant-scoped;
    prunes via (site_id, timestamp), secondary sort by distinct_id matches
    the source's ORDER BY. Faithful 1:1 port of api/routes/sessions.js:48-61
    (queryName 'sessions_conversions'). Identity rule #19a: distinct_id is
    the row-grouping key downstream (canonical stitching key), no
    argMin/argMax. Typed-column translation (SCOPE_v3.md §2.6):
    properties.site_id -> site_id, event -> event_type,
    properties.conversion_value -> conversion_value (typed Float64 DEFAULT 0,
    NOT Nullable). No JSON-bag fields.
    Date range REQUIRED (same as sessions_pageviews.pipe) — ported as
    required params date_from_ts/date_to_ts.
    NOT YET PUSHED — validated read-only via `tb --cloud sql` only.
    DEPLOY FIX (tb --cloud deploy --check, ST_Staging v4.6.4): date/datetime
    params were declared String(param, required=True) then wrapped in
    toDateTime(...) — that combination failed with CANNOT_PARSE_DATETIME
    under --check's '__no_value__' placeholder injection (a non-date string
    toDateTime() can't parse). Fixed by declaring the param itself as
    DateTime(...) (matching the already-shipped Phase 4 pipes' proven
    pattern) and dropping the now-redundant toDateTime(...) wrapper — no
    SQL/filter logic changed, only the param type. Re-validated via
    tb --cloud sql with real values post-fix; parity held (see batch
    dispatch report).

NODE sessions_conversions_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        distinct_id,
        timestamp,
        conversion_value
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND event_type = '$conversion'
      AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(date_from_ts, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp < {{ DateTime(date_to_ts, required=True) }}
    ORDER BY distinct_id ASC, timestamp ASC
    LIMIT 50000

TYPE endpoint
